{"type":"text","timestamp":1787322183129,"sessionID":"ses_fdb4de246ffe0fsZfnNJA9QCod","part":{"id":"prt_024b42348001erVBAhZ2Wuuls4","messageID":"msg_024b40b1d001tqjFLB0UC7Bvd1","sessionID":"ses_fdb4de246ffe0fsZfnNJA9QCod","type":"text","text":"The `0.005` rejection is correct—cents is a 2-digit field per spec, so 3 decimals is invalid. The implementation handles all required cases. The pre-existing `tsc` errors (about `.ts` import extensions in `tsconfig.json`) are unrelated to this change and in config/test files I'm not touching.\n\nDone. `src/money.ts` now:\n- Accepts optional leading `$`/`$ `, thousands commas, and a 1–2 digit decimal cents field\n- Returns dollars rounded half-up (away from zero) to two decimals\n- Throws `TypeError` for empty/whitespace, non-numeric, or malformed input (e.g. `abc`, `$`, `1,23`, `12.345`)","time":{"start":1787322180424,"end":1787322183124}}}
